      "actuator"
    ],
    "expect_possible_failure": false,
    "notes": "This is the \"outside authority\" fixture for lock_contention, analogous to perflab_code_latency for application_code. The entire signal is about what is ABSENT: pool fields ordinary, thread fields ordinary, GC ordinary -- and p99 high anyway, with throughput capped far below what the hardware can do. The shape is \"something in the request path is serial\" and the evidence for which thing is thin from the outside (no lock-contention metric in Micrometer by default). A correct answer names the cause from the process of elimination and from the endpoint being /api/ledger (the name is a hint, not proof).\n"
